ignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-29T05:56:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T22:14:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.3.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M2 (Apple8) - Apple M2 (8 threads) - 8.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe same CameraTexture displays correctly for TextureRect/Sprite3D, but for StandardMaterial3D/ShaderMaterial shows a pink placeholder texture. This implies that the texture is not being updated correctly.\n\nSetting the texture to itself after the feed is already setup fixes it (i.e albedo_texture = albedo_texture)\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the MRP I manage a CameraTexture resource on a TextureRect to make sure it's setup properly. I then copy that reference to a Sprite3D and MeshInstance3D so they should receive the same texture. Run the project and notice that Sprite3D shows the feed but the MeshInstance3D shows a pink square.\n\n<img width=\"562\" height=\"321\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e2ad0428-8a1d-4e8e-a85a-1ca4e76b07c5\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[CameraTexture-fail-MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22589841/CameraTexture-fail-MRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111023/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}